Subject: [M150] [Editing] Copy id attribute when undoing a split

Original change's description:
> [Editing] Copy id attribute when undoing a split
>
> Undoing a split recovered the original element's id by holding a
> reference returned from FastGetAttribute(). That reference points into
> the source element's attribute storage, which the following
> setAttribute() call can reallocate: setting the id notifies id
> observers, which may run script that mutates the source element's
> attributes before the value is consumed.
>
> Hold an owning AtomicString instead. This matches the ownership already
> used in Element::InsertedInto() and Element::RemovedFrom().
>
> Bug: 570638833, 572546688
